---
/**
 * CaseSrikanth.astro
 *
 * Case study 02. Srikanth Engineering Works, Hyderabad. One headline
 * number (47%), one moment, one pull-quote, one DashboardDoodle.
 * Source copy in content/04-case-srikanth-turnaround.md.
 */

import DashboardDoodle from '~/components/ui/DashboardDoodle.astro';

interface Props {}
---

<section id="case-srikanth" class="section case">
  <div class="container-x case-container">
    <div class="case-doodle" aria-hidden="true">
      <DashboardDoodle size={150} float={true} />
    </div>
    <p class="eyebrow case-eyebrow">case study 02 · 2019 to 2023 · project manager</p>

    <h2 id="case-srikanth-h" class="h-section case-heading">
      The <span class="hl">12-KPI dashboard</span>.
    </h2>

    <p class="case-meta">Srikanth Engineering Works, Hyderabad. 300-person agri-tech.</p>

    <div class="case-metric" id="case-srikanth-metric">
      <span class="case-metric-value">47%</span>
      <span class="case-metric-label">bottlenecks cut in three months</span>
    </div>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="case-row">
        <svg class="case-glyph" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 32 32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none">
          {/* Question mark — chaotic problem state */}
          <path d="M 10.4 11.3 C 10.6 7.4 13.7 5.6 16 5.6 C 19.3 5.6 21.7 8.4 21.6 11.4 C 21.4 14.6 16 14.7 16 18.6" />
          <circle cx="16" cy="23" r="1.6" fill="#111" stroke="none" />
        </svg>
        <p>
          I joined Srikanth in June 2019. The senior team was reading five separate weekly reports, one per business unit, each in its own format, all arriving on different days. By the time leadership saw a problem, the problem had already cost the business something material.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-row">
        <svg class="case-glyph" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 32 32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none">
          {/* Clock — weekly Monday rituals */}
          <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="11.4" />
          <path d="M16 16 L 16 9.4" />
          <path d="M16 16 L 21.3 18.4" />
        </svg>
        <p>
          Three months in, the five reports were dead. In their place: a 12-KPI weekly review the senior team finished in 45 minutes, every Monday at 10am, same agenda every time. The biggest bottlenecks turned out to live between finance and ops, not inside either function, so I rebuilt the handoff between them with clear ownership, weekly check-ins, and a shared definition of done. Bottlenecks fell 47% in a quarter. By month four I had also cut the review itself from 20 KPIs down to 12.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="case-row">
        <svg class="case-glyph" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 32 32" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" fill="none">
          {/* Check in circle — consistency outcome */}
          <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="11.4" />
          <path d="M10.6 16.3 L 14.4 19.7 L 21.4 12.4" />
        </svg>
        <p>
          Eighteen months of weekly senior reports followed. Zero missed deadlines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <blockquote id="case-srikanth-quote" class="case-quote">
      The KPI that matters is the one that triggers an action. Removing eight vanity KPIs made the dashboard sharper, not weaker.
    </blockquote>

    <p class="case-tags">5 BUs · 300 employees · 35% efficiency gain · 28% cycle compression · 30% process improvement · 18 months zero missed deadlines</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .case {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ms-border-subtle);
  }

  .case-container {
    position: relative;
  }

  .case-doodle {
    display: none;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .case-doodle {
      display: block;
      position: absolute;
      right: var(--space-7);
      top: var(--space-6);
    }
  }

  .case-eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .case-heading {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
    color: var(--ms-fg-1);
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .case-meta {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-7) 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ms-fg-3);
  }

  .case-metric {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
  }

  .case-metric-value {
    font-family: var(--ms-font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(80px, 12vw, 140px);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    color: var(--ms-fg-1);
  }

  .case-metric-label {
    font-family: var(--ms-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ms-fg-2);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .case-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: 64ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-7);
    color: var(--ms-fg-2);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .case-body p {
    margin: 0;
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .case-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .case-glyph {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    margin-top: 6px;
    color: var(--ms-fg-1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .case-row {
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }
    .case-glyph {
      width: 28px;
      height: 28px;
    }
  }

  .case-quote {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-7) 0;
    padding: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    border: 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--ms-accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.4vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ms-fg-1);
    max-width: 38ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .case-tags {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 64ch;
    font-family: var(--ms-font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ms-fg-3);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
